Package: nonBgfa
Title: Detection of Non-B DNA-Forming Motifs in DNA Sequences
Version: 0.2.0
Author: Aqsa Azhar [cre, aut],
    Duncan E. Donohue [aut, cph] (Original GFA algorithm),
    Jack R. Collins [aut, cph] (Original GFA algorithm)
Maintainer: Aqsa Azhar <azhar@example.com>
Description:
    The nonBgfa package provides tools for detecting non-B DNA-forming
    motifs in genomic sequences. Non-B DNA structures include cruciform,
    triplex, slipped (hairpin) structures, tetraplex (G-quadruplex),
    left-handed Z-DNA, and others. These structures may play roles in
    DNA instability and mutagenesis, leading to DNA rearrangements and
    increased mutational rates, which are hallmarks of cancer.
    .
    This package wraps the GFA (Genomic Feature Analyzer) C code,
    originally developed at NCI-Frederick/Frederick National Lab,
    providing an R interface for detecting sequences associated with
    non-B DNA forming motifs.
